# Astraphe AI — Frontend Design System

## Design Language: "Spectral" Glassmorphism

Astraphe uses a **dark-first, translucent aesthetic** — layered depth, continuous gradient meshes, surgical accent colors. Every screen should feel like a data terminal floating in deep space. Never produce generic, flat, or "light-mode-ported-dark" UI.

### Core Principles

- **Elevation via opacity** — higher cards use higher background opacity. Never use blur except on modal overlays (performance constraint on 60 Hz mobile panels).
- **Surgical illumination** — accent glows are applied to at most ONE primary element per screen. Overuse destroys hierarchy.
- **Data density with breathing room** — pack metrics tightly but always preserve clear visual rhythm through consistent spacing.
- **Mono for data, Grotesk for prose** — all numeric/metric values use `font-mono`; labels, headings, and body copy use `font-sans` (Space Grotesk).

---

## Design Tokens

Always use Tailwind utility classes for color. Never hardcode hex values or `rgba()` literals in `class=""` attributes. CSS variables (`var(--*)`) are valid only in `style=""` attributes and `<style>` blocks — **never** in Tailwind class strings.

### Backgrounds / Surfaces (Tailwind → CSS var → hex)

| Tailwind | CSS var | Hex | Usage |
|----------|---------|-----|-------|
| `bg-bg0` | `--bg0` | `#08080F` | Deepest layer, page background |
| `bg-bg1` | `--bg1` | `#0F0F1A` | Section backgrounds |
| `bg-bg2` | `--bg2` | `#141424` | Card backgrounds |
| `bg-bg3` | `--bg3` | `#1C1C30` | Elevated cards, code blocks |
| `bg-glass` | `--glass` | `rgba(255,255,255,0.04)` | Standard card surface |
| `bg-glass2` | `--glass2` | `rgba(255,255,255,0.08)` | Elevated / interactive surface |
| `border-border` | `--border` | `rgba(255,255,255,0.07)` | All card and divider borders |

### Accent Colors

| Tailwind | CSS var | Hex | Usage |
|----------|---------|-----|-------|
| `text-blue` / `bg-blue` / `border-blue` | `--blue` | `#4621FF` | Primary CTA, active states, fitness |
| `bg-blue-dim` | — | `rgba(70,33,255,0.15)` | Selected card backgrounds |
| `border-blue-glow` | — | `rgba(70,33,255,0.3)` | Active card border glow |
| `text-teal` / `bg-teal` / `border-teal` | `--teal` | `#00C8A8` | Success, HRV, recovery |
| `bg-teal-dim` | — | `rgba(0,200,168,0.15)` | Positive state backgrounds |
| `text-amber` / `bg-amber` / `border-amber` | `--amber` | `#FFCB88` | Warnings, ATL effort, load |
| `bg-amber-dim` | — | `rgba(255,203,136,0.15)` | Caution state backgrounds |
| `text-red` / `bg-red` / `border-red` | `--red` | `#F07178` | Alerts, max HR, danger |
| `bg-red-dim` | — | `rgba(240,113,120,0.15)` | Alert state backgrounds |

### Text Hierarchy

| Tailwind | CSS var | Value | Usage |
|----------|---------|-------|-------|
| `text-text0` | `--text0` | `#F0F0FF` | Primary text |
| `text-text1` | `--text1` | `rgba(240,240,255,0.65)` | Secondary text, labels |
| `text-text2` | `--text2` | `rgba(240,240,255,0.35)` | Placeholders, metadata, disabled |

**`text-text3` does not exist** — use `text-text2` for the most muted text.

### Zone Colors (HR Zones — CSS variable only)

Zone colors exist **only as CSS variables** — there are no Tailwind utilities for them. Use `var(--zone-n)` in `style=""` attributes or canvas `fillStyle`. Never use a zone color as a UI accent.

| CSS var | Hex | Zone |
|---------|-----|------|
| `--zone-0` | `#94a3b8` | Zone 0 / rest |
| `--zone-1` | `#579BFA` | Zone 1 — light perceptual blue, **distinct from `--blue` (`#4621FF`)** |
| `--zone-2` | `#00C8A8` | Zone 2 |
| `--zone-3` | `#FFCB88` | Zone 3 |
| `--zone-4` | `#FF8C42` | Zone 4 |
| `--zone-5` | `#F07178` | Zone 5 |

Usage in templates:
```svelte
<!-- Zone color on a DOM element -->
<div style="color: var(--zone-1)">Z1</div>

<!-- Zone color in Tailwind arbitrary value (only when no style= is available) -->
<div class="bg-[color:var(--zone-1)]">Z1</div>

<!-- Canvas — must use hex from HR_ZONE_HEX constant, not var(--zone-n) -->
ctx.fillStyle = HR_ZONE_HEX[1]; // '#579BFA'
```

### Training Load Chart Colors

These are chart-specific identity tokens, separate from the semantic accent palette. Use hex constants from `$lib/scoreColors.ts` for canvas/LayerChart; use Tailwind classes for DOM legend swatches only.

| Token | Hex | Tailwind (DOM only) | Usage |
|-------|-----|---------------------|-------|
| `CHART_CTL_STROKE` | `#3b82f6` | `text-chartCtl` / `stroke-chartCtl` | CTL (fitness) line |
| `CHART_ATL_STROKE` | `#334155` | `text-chartAtl` / `stroke-chartAtl` | ATL (fatigue) line |

```ts
// scoreColors.ts — import these for canvas and LayerChart props
import { CHART_CTL_STROKE, CHART_ATL_STROKE } from '$lib/scoreColors';
// DOM legend swatch only:
// class="bg-chartCtl" or class="bg-chartAtl"
```

### Brand Namespace

`astraphe.*` tokens exist in Tailwind config as aliases. Prefer the semantic tokens above; use `astraphe-*` only for cross-platform brand consistency requirements.

