## Tailwind Conventions

### Opacity Modifiers — Multiples of 5 Only

Tailwind v3 utility opacity modifiers must be multiples of 5 (`/5`, `/10`, `/15`, `/20`, `/25`, `/30`, `/40`, `/50`, etc.). **Non-standard steps like `/12`, `/35`, `/45` will not compile** unless added to the safelist (not configured).

```svelte
<!-- ✅ Correct -->
<div class="bg-blue/10 border-teal/30 from-blue/10 to-teal/5">

<!-- ❌ Will not compile -->
<div class="bg-blue/12 border-red/35 from-blue/45">

<!-- ✅ Use arbitrary rgba for exact non-standard opacities -->
<div class="border-[rgba(240,113,120,0.35)] from-[rgba(70,33,255,0.12)]">
```

### No Hardcoded Colors in Class Attributes

```svelte
<!-- ❌ Wrong — arbitrary hex in class -->
<div class="text-[#4621FF] bg-[#08080F] border-[rgba(255,255,255,0.07)]">

<!-- ✅ Correct — Tailwind tokens -->
<div class="text-blue bg-bg0 border-border">
```

### Standard Tailwind Palette is Forbidden for UI

Never use `slate-*`, `gray-*`, `zinc-*`, `indigo-*`, `white`, `black`, `blue-500`, `red-300`, etc. as UI colors. Map everything to Astraphe tokens:

| Forbidden | Astraphe replacement |
|-----------|---------------------|
| `text-white`, `text-slate-100/200` | `text-text0` |
| `text-slate-300/400` | `text-text1` |
| `text-slate-500/600` | `text-text2` |
| `bg-slate-900/950` | `bg-bg0` / `bg-bg1` |
| `bg-slate-800`, `bg-slate-800/40` | `bg-bg2` or `bg-glass2` |
| `border-slate-700/800` | `border-border` |
| `bg-black/60`, `bg-black/80` | `bg-bg0/60`, `bg-bg0/80` |
| `bg-white/5`, `ring-white/[0.12]` | `bg-glass`, `ring-border` |
| `text-indigo-*`, `bg-indigo-*` | `text-blue`, `bg-blue-dim`, `border-blue/30` |
| `text-blue-500` | `text-blue` |
| `text-red-300/400` | `text-red` |

**Exception:** Third-party brand colors (Strava `#FC4C02`, Garmin `#009CDE`, Apple, WHOOP) and sport-type colors with no Astraphe equivalent (`#a855f7` mobility, `#eab308` other) are kept as hex literals with a comment.

### CSS Variables in Tailwind Class Strings

`var(--*)` does not work inside Tailwind utility strings. Use `style=""` for CSS variable application:

```svelte
<!-- ❌ Wrong -->
<div class="text-[var(--teal)]">

<!-- ✅ Correct — use Tailwind token -->
<div class="text-teal">

<!-- ✅ Correct — use style for dynamic/zone vars where no token exists -->
<div style="color: var(--zone-2)">
```

### Canvas, D3, Mapbox, and SVG Presentation Attributes

CSS variables **do not resolve** in any of these contexts. Always use hex literals or constants from `scoreColors.ts`:

| Context | Rule |
|---------|------|
| Canvas `fillStyle` / `strokeStyle` | Hex only — `'#4621FF'` or `CHART_CTL_STROKE` |
| D3 `.attr('stroke', c)` / `.attr('fill', c)` | Hex only |
| Mapbox GL `paint: { 'line-color': … }` | Hex only |
| SVG `stroke={color}` / `fill={color}` (presentation attributes) | Hex only |
| `{@html}` SVG template string `stroke="${c}"` | Hex only |
| SVG `style="stroke: var(--blue)"` | CSS var valid here only |
| DOM `class="text-blue"` | Tailwind token |

```svelte
<!-- ❌ Renders as black — var() in canvas/D3/Mapbox -->
ctx.fillStyle = 'var(--blue)';
.attr('stroke', 'var(--teal)')
paint: { 'line-color': 'var(--blue)' }

<!-- ✅ Correct -->
ctx.fillStyle = '#4621FF';
.attr('stroke', '#00C8A8')
paint: { 'line-color': '#4621FF' }
```

