## Chart / Data Visualization

Using **LayerChart** (D3-backed SVG). Key conventions:

- Area charts: gradient fill using `LinearGradient` with accent color at `opacity: 0.25` → `0`
- Line strokes: `strokeWidth={2}`, accent color
- Axis ticks: `font-mono`, `text-text2`, `text-[10px]`
- Always DPR-scale canvas elements manually (`devicePixelRatio`)

### Metric-to-color mapping

| Metric | Semantic color | DOM class | Canvas/chart |
|--------|----------------|-----------|--------------|
| HRV / Recovery | teal | `text-teal` | `'#00C8A8'` |
| CTL (fitness) | chartCtl | `text-chartCtl` | `CHART_CTL_STROKE` |
| ATL (fatigue load) | chartAtl | `text-chartAtl` | `CHART_ATL_STROKE` |
| ATL (effort/UI) | amber | `text-amber` | `'#FFCB88'` |
| TSB (form) positive | teal | `text-teal` | `'#00C8A8'` |
| TSB (form) negative | red | `text-red` | `'#F07178'` |
| HR / effort | red | `text-red` | `'#F07178'` |
| HR zones | zone vars | `style="color: var(--zone-n)"` | `HR_ZONE_HEX[n]` |

### Gradient Card Backgrounds

```svelte
<!-- Static gradient — Tailwind v3, opacity must be multiple of 5 -->
<Card class="bg-gradient-to-br from-blue/10 via-transparent to-teal/5">

<!-- Non-standard opacity — use arbitrary rgba -->
<Card class="bg-gradient-to-br from-[rgba(70,33,255,0.12)] via-transparent to-teal/5">

<!-- Dynamic gradient — keep inline style -->
<div style="background: linear-gradient(135deg, {color}22, transparent)">
```

